---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Workforce AI Training — Nairon"
  description="Train your operators, dispatchers, coordinators, and back-office teams to work alongside AI employees. Hands-on training tailored to your workflows and tools, on-site or remote."
  eyebrow="AI Training"
  heading="Workforce AI Training"
  intro="Your AI employees do real operational work. This program upskills your whole team to work alongside them &mdash; delegating tasks, reviewing output, and finding the next thing to automate."
>
  <div class="page-body">
    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">Who it's for</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">The people who run day-to-day operations and now share the work with AI employees.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-2">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Operations</div>
          <h3>Operators &amp; managers</h3>
          <p>The people accountable for throughput and quality. They set what AI employees own and where a human stays in the loop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Field &amp; scheduling</div>
          <h3>Dispatchers &amp; coordinators</h3>
          <p>The people scheduling jobs, routing crews, and handling resident and customer requests alongside their AI employees.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Back office</div>
          <h3>Back-office teams</h3>
          <p>The people handling permits, quoting, follow-ups, and other administrative work that AI employees now do a first pass on.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">New hires</div>
          <h3>Anyone joining the team</h3>
          <p>New staff who need to be productive with AI employees from day one, not months later.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">What your team learns</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">Practical skills for working with AI employees inside the tools you already use.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-2">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Day to day</div>
          <h3>Working with AI employees</h3>
          <p>How AI employees fit into daily operations, what they own, what they hand back, and how to work with them inside your CRM, scheduling, and inbox.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Delegation</div>
          <h3>Prompting &amp; delegating tasks</h3>
          <p>How to hand off work clearly &mdash; scoping a task, giving the right context, and setting expectations so the AI employee returns usable results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Quality</div>
          <h3>Reviewing &amp; correcting agent work</h3>
          <p>How to check an AI employee's output, catch mistakes, correct course, and use the audit trail to see exactly what was done and why.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Growth</div>
          <h3>Spotting where to automate next</h3>
          <p>How to recognize repetitive, rules-based work that an AI employee could take on next, and how to bring it to Nairon to build.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">Format</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">Hands-on and built around how your team actually works.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-3">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Hands-on</div>
          <h3>Learning by doing</h3>
          <p>Your team works through real tasks with their own AI employees, not slides. People leave having done the work, not just watched it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Tailored</div>
          <h3>Your workflows &amp; tools</h3>
          <p>The training uses your systems, your processes, and the AI employees we built for you &mdash; so what your team practices is what they do the next day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Flexible</div>
          <h3>On-site or remote</h3>
          <p>Delivered at your location or over video, whichever fits your team. We scope the length and structure to your operation during the audit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <h2 class="page-section-title">Outcomes</h2>
      <p class="page-section-sub">A team that owns its AI employees and keeps extending them.</p>
      <div class="page-grid cols-2">
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Confidence</div>
          <h3>Your team owns the work</h3>
          <p>Operators, dispatchers, coordinators, and back-office staff are confident delegating to their AI employees and reviewing what comes back.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="page-card">
          <div class="page-card-kicker">Momentum</div>
          <h3>Your team extends it</h3>
          <p>Instead of waiting on us for every change, your team spots the next task to automate and brings it forward &mdash; so the AI workforce grows with the business.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:24px;">Training is scoped during your AI audit, alongside the Discover, Build, Tune, and Enable work that stands up your AI employees.</p>
      <a href="/#book" style="align-items:center; background-color:#0f6bd4; border-radius:40px; color:#fff; display:inline-flex; font-family:'Geist',system-ui,sans-serif; font-size:15px; font-weight:500; gap:8px; margin-top:8px; padding:13px 24px; text-decoration:none;">Book an AI audit <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Page>
